empty tool argument streams are reported as a missing bash command

## Symptom
The missing-command error is also manufactured by our parsers.

- `provider_anthropic.ml` finalize replaces an empty argument buffer with `"{}"`.
- `provider_minimax.ml` does the same.
- Responses streaming (`provider_openai_codex.ml` `output_item.added` / `output_item.done`) stores the call id and name and ignores `item.arguments`. If the provider sends the full arguments only on those events, the buffer stays empty.
- Validation then reports that the model forgot `command`, and B622 asks the model to re-emit the same call.

## Decision
An empty or dropped argument stream is a transport failure, not a schema miss.

- Do not rewrite `""` to `"{}"`.
- Keep arguments that arrived on Anthropic `content_block.input` (already partially handled) and on Responses `item.arguments` for `output_item.added` and `output_item.done`.
- When the final argument string is empty, return an error that says the argument stream was empty and includes the tool name. Do not use the missing-required-parameter text, so the model is not told to re-emit the same shape.
- MiniMax gets the same empty-buffer treatment as Anthropic.

## Lane
Depends on B819. Same files (`provider_anthropic.ml`, Responses flattener). Serial, after B819 is merged. Do not parallelize.

## Acceptance
- Anthropic stream finalize of a tool_use block with no input and no input_json_delta does not produce `"{}"`.
- The resulting tool call is a transport error, not `missing required parameter 'command'`.
- A content_block_start that embeds a non-empty `input` object still preserves it.
- Responses `output_item.done` / `output_item.added` with `item.arguments` seeds the argument buffer.
- A later empty completed item does not wipe a buffer that already holds valid JSON.
- MiniMax empty stream follows the same rule.
- Tests cover these cases. `make test` passes.